RESEARCH REFLECTION for masked_contact_stats_deepsets_head_idea3_001:
Conclusion  : Good (first scored run, so it is the best so far by default). lr_auprc 0.569 is slightly above the hypothesized 0.4-0.6 range and far above the 0.11 random level. Secondary metrics support this: lr_auroc 0.894 and direction_accuracy 0.817. No baseline or best score was supplied, so the Spearman-baseline comparison is not verified. Trial_portion is 1.0, so the score is not low-data noise.
Key Factor  : The default masked contact-stats DeepSets head, with closed-form rank statistics as input. It is a tiny model (1617 params) trained with smooth_l1 for 15 epochs at full data portion.
Discovery   : A very small model on closed-form rank statistics already gives strong ranking signal, which supports the hypothesis that the statistics carry most of the signal. Training was healthy: train loss fell 0.0344 to 0.0233, and validation fell 0.0259 to 0.0241 with a small train-val gap of +0.0008. Validation was noisy, with a spike at epoch 7 (0.0252) and a rebound at the last epoch (0.0241 vs best 0.0228 at epoch 14 in 1-indexed terms). The selected checkpoint was best_validation_loss, so the final-epoch rebound did not affect the evaluated model. The data does not show overfitting. It does show late-epoch validation instability, which is a mild concern about lr or batch noise. Train loss was still creeping down slowly at epoch 15, so the run may not be fully converged. The score gates passed: 10 distinct symbols, and the dominant tie fraction was 0.10.
Memory Update: Treat this config (score 0.569, auprc; smooth_l1 final loss 0.0233; 1617 params; 15 epochs) as the reference point for later runs. Before changing the architecture, check three things. (1) Get the Spearman baseline lr_auprc on the same eval set. Without it, the claim of beating the baseline is unverified. (2) Repeat with a different seed to estimate run-to-run variance. Differences below 0.02 are unresolved. (3) Test one-factor changes: lower lr or a lr decay to damp the validation oscillation, and more epochs (e.g. 30), since train loss was still slowly falling. Do not compare loss values against runs with a different loss_type. Larger models are not justified until they beat 0.569 by more than 0.02. The small 1617-param model is a strong candidate for the efficient reference in the Solidification phase.
