RESEARCH REFLECTION for masked_contact_stats_deepsets_head_idea3_002:
Conclusion  : Marginally good: lr_auprc 0.5765 is the new best, above the previous best of 0.5687 (+0.0078, about +1.4%). There is no baseline score. This is a Formal round at full data (portion 1.0), but the gain is small and is probably within seed and run noise. The same-loss (smooth_l1) final train loss, 0.02278, is also the lowest seen, versus 0.02330 before. Secondary metrics are healthy: lr_auroc 0.897 and direction_accuracy 0.817. Health gates passed.
Key Factor  : The executed config is the inherited winner's config: 15 epochs, lr 0.002 decaying to about 0.00045 across the run, adamw, smooth_l1, 1617 params. The cosine-style learning-rate decay is the only visible difference from the prior best. The proposed 20 epochs was overruled to 15 and did not run, so none of this result can be credited to a longer schedule.
Discovery   : With 15 epochs and the lr decayed from 0.002 to 0.00045, training and validation losses fall together. Train went 0.0337 to 0.0228 and validation 0.0280 to 0.0227. The train-validation gap is about zero (-5e-5), so a 1617-param model is not overfitting. Validation was best at epoch 12 (0.02238, one-based) and drifted up only +0.00034 afterward, and it is noisy from epoch 13 on. That points to a plateau, not clear underfit or overfit. Checkpoint selection by best validation loss correctly picked the epoch-12 weights. Train loss was still slowly decreasing at the end, but validation was flat, so extra epochs would likely add little. Loss differences of about 0.0005 map to AUPRC differences of about 0.008, which is a weak link.
Memory Update: Treat 0.5765 as the new best (exp idea3_002: embed16/phi16/hidden32, lr 0.002 with decay, 15 epochs, batch 32, smooth_l1, 1617 params). It is only about +0.008 over idea3_001, so it is not clearly separable from noise. The 20-epoch hypothesis was never tested because epochs were locked to 15, so do not record it as refuted. Gap is about 0, so capacity is not the bottleneck by the overfitting measure. Validation plateaued at epochs 10-15, so more epochs is unlikely to help. Next, vary something other than epochs: modestly larger embed_dim, phi_hidden_dim or hidden_dim, or more n_stats. Other options are min_contacts or ridge_lambda, which change the masked contact statistics, and weight_decay or dropout. Confirm any gain of under about 0.01 with a repeat seed. Data scope is operator-fixed at formal_portion 1.0, so do not recommend changing trial_portion.
